{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<cstdio>\n#include<cstring>\n#include<algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MOD = 1e9+7;\n#define LL long long\n\nstruct matrix{\n\tint A[31][31],N;\n\t\n\tmatrix operator *(const matrix &B)const{\n\t\tmatrix C; C.N = N; \n\t\tfor(int i = 0 ; i <= N ; ++i)\n\t\t\tfor(int j = 0 ; j <= N ; ++j){\n\t\t\t\tC.A[i][j] = 0;\n\t\t\t\tfor(int k = 0 ; k <= N ; ++k)\n\t\t\t\t\tC.A[i][j] = ((LL)A[i][k]*B.A[k][j] + C.A[i][j])%MOD;\n\t\t\t}\n\t\treturn C;\n\t}\n}A[64][30],sum[64][30],suf[64][30],ans;\n\nLL N,K,dig[70],cnt;\n\nint main(){\n\tscanf(\"%lld%lld\",&N,&K);\n\twhile(N){dig[cnt++] = N % K; N /= K;}\n\tfor(int i = 0 ; i < K ; ++i){\n\t\tfor(int j = 0 ; j <= K ; ++j)\n\t\t\tA[0][i].A[j][j] = 1,A[0][i].A[j][i] = 1;\n\t\tA[0][i].N = K;\n\t}\n\tsum[0][0] = A[0][0]; suf[0][K-1] = A[0][K-1];\n\tfor(int i = 1 ; i < K ; ++i) sum[0][i] = sum[0][i-1]*A[0][i];\n\tfor(int i = K - 2; ~i ; --i) suf[0][i] = A[0][i]*suf[0][i+1];\n\tfor(int i = 1 ; i < cnt ; ++i){\n\t\tA[i][0] = suf[i-1][0];\n\t\tfor(int j = 1 ; j < K ; ++j)\n\t\t\tA[i][j] = suf[i-1][j]*sum[i-1][j-1];\n\t\tsum[i][0] = A[i][0]; suf[i][K-1] = A[i][K-1];\n\t\tfor(int j = 1 ; j < K ; ++j) sum[i][j] = sum[i][j-1]*A[i][j];\n\t\tfor(int j = K - 2 ; ~j; --j) suf[i][j] = A[i][j]*suf[i][j+1];\n\t}\n\tans.A[0][K] = 1; ans.N = K;\n\tans = ans*sum[cnt-1][dig[cnt-1] - 1];\n\tint last = dig[cnt-1];\n\tfor(int i = cnt - 2 ; ~i ; --i){\n\t\tfor(int j = 0 ; j < dig[i] ; ++j)\t\n\t\t\tans = ans*A[i][(j+last)%K];\n\t\tlast += dig[i];\n\t}\n\tLL res = 0;\n\tfor(int i = 0 ; i <= K ; ++i) res = res + ans.A[0][i];\n\tprintf(\"%lld\\n\",res%MOD);\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B, size):\n    C = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for i in range(size):\n        for k in range(size):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(size):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    N = int(data[0])\n    K = int(data[1])\n    \n    # digits in base K, least significant first\n    dig = []\n    while N:\n        dig.append(N % K)\n        N //= K\n    cnt = len(dig)\n    if cnt == 0:\n        print(0)\n        return\n    \n    size = K + 1\n    \n    # A[0][i] for i in 0..K-1\n    A0 = []\n    for i in range(K):\n        mat = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n        for j in range(size):\n            mat[j][j] = 1\n            mat[j][i] = 1\n        A0.append(mat)\n    \n    # sum[0] and suf[0]\n    sum0 = [None] * K\n    suf0 = [None] * K\n    sum0[0] = A0[0]\n    for i in range(1, K):\n        sum0[i] = mat_mul(sum0[i-1], A0[i], size)\n    suf0[K-1] = A0[K-1]\n    for i in range(K-2, -1, -1):\n        suf0[i] = mat_mul(A0[i], suf0[i+1], size)\n    \n    # store all levels\n    A = [A0]\n    sum_list = [sum0]\n    suf_list = [suf0]\n    \n    for level in range(1, cnt):\n        prev_suf = suf_list[level-1]\n        prev_sum = sum_list[level-1]\n        A_lev = [None] * K\n        A_lev[0] = prev_suf[0]\n        for j in range(1, K):\n            A_lev[j] = mat_mul(prev_suf[j], prev_sum[j-1], size)\n        # compute sum and suf for this level\n        sum_lev = [None] * K\n        suf_lev = [None] * K\n        sum_lev[0] = A_lev[0]\n        for j in range(1, K):\n            sum_lev[j] = mat_mul(sum_lev[j-1], A_lev[j], size)\n        suf_lev[K-1] = A_lev[K-1]\n        for j in range(K-2, -1, -1):\n            suf_lev[j] = mat_mul(A_lev[j], suf_lev[j+1], size)\n        A.append(A_lev)\n        sum_list.append(sum_lev)\n        suf_list.append(suf_lev)\n    \n    # initial ans: row vector with 1 at column K\n    ans = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    ans[0][K] = 1\n    \n    # multiply by sum of most significant digit\n    most_sig = dig[cnt-1]\n    ans = mat_mul(ans, sum_list[cnt-1][most_sig - 1], size)\n    \n    last = most_sig\n    for i in range(cnt-2, -1, -1):\n        d = dig[i]\n        for j in range(d):\n            ans = mat_mul(ans, A[i][(j + last) % K], size)\n        last += d\n    \n    res = sum(ans[0][i] for i in range(size)) % MOD\n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -9.405170567333698e-05, -0.21199488639831543, -0.0002613918040879071, -0.008615939877927303, -2.753696753643453e-05, 0.0, -1.9192511899746023e-05, -0.04883621260523796, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.00010334911348763853, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.887569048150908e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, 0.0, -3.099436753473128e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -1.3112935448589269e-05, -0.0018887552432715893, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.5787225961685181, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -0.018150078132748604, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0